{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Five hundred years old.</b> Rabbi Yudan said: What is the reason — all the generations fathered children at one hundred, but this one at five hundred? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: If they are wicked, they will perish in the waters, and that is bad for this righteous man; and if they are righteous, I burden him to build many arks. He held back his fountain and did not father children until five hundred years, so that Japheth, the eldest of his sons, would not be liable to punishments before the Flood (Bereshit Rabbah). For it is written ״כִּי הַנַּעַר בֶּן מֵאָה שָׁנָה יָמוּת״ (Isaiah 65) — liable to punishment in the future, and likewise before the giving of the Torah." "<b>Shem, Ham, and Japheth.</b> But is Japheth not the eldest? Rather, at the outset you expound upon the one who is righteous, born circumcised, and from whom Abraham would come, etc. — in Bereshit Rabbah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:41.245997541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}